A soft drink was bottled with a partial pressure of $\mathrm{CO}_2$ of 3 bar over the liquid at room temperature. The partial pressure of $\mathrm{CO}_2$ over the solution approaches a value of 30 bar when $44\ \mathrm{g}$ of $\mathrm{CO}_2$ is dissolved in $1\ \mathrm{kg}$ of water at room temperature. The approximate $\mathrm{pH}$ of the soft drink is ________ $\times 10^{-1}$ .
(First dissociation constant of $\mathrm{H}_2\mathrm{CO}_3=4.0\times10^{-7}$ ;
$\log 2=0.3;$ density of the soft drink $=1\ \mathrm{g}\ \mathrm{mL}^{-1} )$
